# Caddy fronts itervox with automatic Let's Encrypt TLS.
#
# Itervox itself has no TLS — there is no ListenAndServeTLS anywhere in
# internal/server/ — so something has to terminate it for a public URL.
#
# Itervox auto-generates an ephemeral bearer token on every bind — including
# loopback — unless ITERVOX_API_TOKEN is pinned or server.allow_unauthenticated
# is set. Bind address is not a security signal: a loopback daemon behind this
# proxy is exactly as internet-exposed as a public bind, and the daemon has no
# way to tell from inside the process. Pin ITERVOX_API_TOKEN so restarts don't
# invalidate saved dashboard sessions. See https://github.com/vnovick/itervox/issues/48
#
# Prefer a private tunnel (GCP IAP / AWS SSM / Azure Bastion) over this file.

@DOMAIN@ {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8090 {
		# The dashboard is SSE-driven. Disable response buffering and let
		# streams stay open indefinitely, otherwise the live board freezes
		# and silently reconnects on a loop.
		flush_interval -1
	}

	encode gzip

	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/itervox.log
		format json
	}
}
